  "initial_prompt": "Review FileBackup's scoped interface breakdown on low, reporting HIGH-RISK findings only. There are 15 attachments, each below 50 KB, with END OF COMPLETE INPUT markers. Confirm the actual basenames/markers and inventory: 25 IF rows (preserved legacy IF001 plus 24 new Drafted), 40 new Drafted LLRs, 41 planned cases, 121 approved SRs, 49 approved SNs, approved frame/assumptions. Read the normative interface bodies plus registry and derived map, not only counts. No tools, repo access, edits or execution. Static advisory review is not approval or implementation evidence.\n\nTask: assess concrete contradictions/missing ownership or wrongly linked contracts that can cause protected data loss, falsely successful recovery, serious containment/credential breach, or an incompatible caller/writer/reader contract. Critique parent requirements/frame only for high risk and label any proposed upstream change. No stylistic comments, routine unfinished N1 schema details, generic missing implementations, lower risks or arbitrary idealized strengthening. No quota, at most four findings, under 1000 words. Each needs IDs and a causal scenario plus smallest correction.\n\nOwner direction: current bounded loop/shared content architecture is reused. Prior dated snapshot published before latest checkpoints, content hash-while-copy, final-dependent superseded relocation, no backup object deletion. Independent PS/bash scripts stay offline and do not call native engine. New interface owner paths are logical DESIGN responsibilities, not claims that Rust modules exist; shared protocol ownership does not create runtime dependencies. verified_by links LLRs; SRs derive through their parents; planned cases directly name IFs. Exact CLI/event/version fields, state identity implementation and platform benchmarks are ordinary N1/N2 design work still open. Do not treat Drafted references as passed tests.\n\nPrevious-definition policy: finish preserving manifest+directory sidecar as .prev before any current definition changes; existing previous copies are never overwritten on later unsuccessful runs. Delete only after successful replacement/finalization. Interruption during copying leaves old current records available; during deletion leaves new current records available. A lone previous file is housekeeping residue, not a failed current state. Default recovery uses valid last-known current records; previous selection is explicit and never mixes sets. Actual missing required metadata on the selected set is diagnosed. No blanket incomplete-run marker, no promise that recoverable checkpoints reflect a completed source scan. Conflicting supplemental directory/link records do not discard safe valid file rows.\n\nFolders/links enter change detection; internal folder links restore relative in-root links; external folder links restore expanded ordinary duplicates with stored-content dedup; file links restore bytes. Managed removal protects latest and retained later dates; external deletion bypasses protocol. Coordination is only within one validated configuration. IF001's original legacy one-set HomeHub OCI agreement is verbatim history, not silently widened by new native IF019; historical labels were archived, rebaseline carrier is Drafted. B11 provisioning is conditional and initially not offered, so no download interface is invented. Approved upstream texts are unchanged. Earlier marker-review conclusions are NOT authority for this scope.\n\nFor any finding distinguish an actual contract contradiction from an explicitly unfinished implementation detail or known accepted residual risk. If none qualifies, say so and state limits; do not invent fixes to satisfy a finding count.",
